# Supabase Camel Case

- When reading data from Supabase, do not expose raw `snake_case` rows to services or UI.
- For list queries, return `listKeysToCamel<T>(response.data || [])`.
- For single-object responses, return `keysToCamel<T>(response.data)` when appropriate.
- Keep `snake_case` only inside the Supabase query itself, table names, selected columns, filters, and other database contracts.
- Prefer converting at the API/integration boundary so hooks, services, and UI consume `camelCase`.

```ts
// Good
const response = await supabase.from(DB_TABLES.PL_STREAMS).select('id, project_id, created_at');
return {
  ...response,
  data: listKeysToCamel<PlStreamDto>(response.data || []),
};
```
